statement:
Let $\alpha$ and $\beta$ be finite index sets, and let $\phi : \alpha \times \beta \to \bbr$ be a real-valued array whose columns are mutually orthogonal with a common squared length: for a fixed constant $c \in \bbr$,
\[
  \sum_{x \in \alpha} \phi(x,y)\,\phi(x,z) = \begin{cases} c & \text{if } y = z,\\ 0 & \text{if } y \neq z,\end{cases}
\]
for all $y, z \in \beta$. Then for any weights $b : \beta \to \bbr$,
\[
  \sum_{x \in \alpha} \Bigl(\sum_{y \in \beta} b(y)\,\phi(x,y)\Bigr)^{2}
  \;=\; c \sum_{y \in \beta} b(y)^{2}.
\]
